"""HUD: one screen saying what this machine is, and what it is doing.

A kiosk page rather than a monitor: it answers the questions that otherwise
take four terminals (df, free, ip, nvidia-smi) and the ones no terminal
answers at a glance, such as which AI agents are running and how much of
their context is spent. Every number comes from hud.py and agents.py, which
read the kernel's files and the agents' own transcripts; this file only draws.

Two modes. The window refreshes every couple of seconds and goes full screen
on F11 or --fullscreen, which is the kiosk. `portlin-hud --json` prints one
snapshot and exits, for scripts, and for the harness, which cannot look at
a window but can read JSON.

The readout's rule holds here: a figure that cannot be known yet is "--",
never a number that looks like the others. The first sample has no rates
and no CPU percentage, and says so.
"""

